        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Amarillo, Texas; Grand Forks, North Dakota; Potter County; Randall County; Grand Forks County\n- Airports: Rick Husband Amarillo International Airport; Grand Forks International Airport\n- Organizations: Texas Air & Space Museum; John D. Odegard School of Aerospace Sciences\n- Codes: IATA AMA; ICAO KAMA; FAA LID AMA; IATA GFK; ICAO KGFK; FAA LID GFK\n- Topics: aviation museums; civilian flight training aircraft\n\nFacts:\n- Rick Husband Amarillo International Airport is a public airport six miles east of downtown Amarillo in Potter and Randall Counties, Texas, United States.\n- Rick Husband Amarillo International Airport has the codes IATA AMA, ICAO KAMA, and FAA LID AMA.\n- Grand Forks International Airport is a public airport five miles northwest of Grand Forks in Grand Forks County, North Dakota.\n- Grand Forks International Airport has the codes IATA GFK, ICAO KGFK, and FAA LID GFK.\n- The Texas Air & Space Museum is an aviation museum located near Rick Husband Amarillo International Airport in Amarillo, Texas.\n- The John D. Odegard School of Aerospace Sciences bases most of its fleet of more than 120 aircraft at Grand Forks International Airport.\n- The John D. Odegard School of Aerospace Sciences operates the largest fleet of civilian flight training aircraft in North America.",
